course: dictionary
lesson: 5651
title: What is a liquid?
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A liquid is something that flows and can be poured, like water, milk or juice. It does not keep its own shape the way a solid does. It takes the shape of whatever holds it.
explain: «In a liquid like juice the particles stay close but slide past each other, so the juice takes the shape of a tall glass or a wide bowl but keeps the same amount.» The juice changes shape, but the amount stays the same. That is one clue that it is a liquid.
explain: Liquid is one of the three main states of matter, with solid and gas. Ice melts into liquid water, and liquid water boils into steam, which is a gas. Liquid can also be an adjective: liquid soap is soap in the form of a liquid.
fact: A liquid flows and can be poured.
fact: Liquid is one of the three states of matter: solid, liquid and gas.
fact: A liquid takes the shape of its container but keeps its volume.
fact: «A skunk can spray a very smelly liquid up to about 3 metres.»
fact: Some liquids are poisons, so never drink from an unmarked bottle.
exercise: What is a liquid? | Something that is always hot | Something hard that keeps its own shape, like a rock | Something you can only see when it is very cold | *Something that flows and can be poured, like water or juice
exercise: Ice melts into liquid water, and liquid water boils into steam. What state of matter is steam? | *A gas | A metal | A liquid | A solid
exercise: «A skunk can spray a very smelly liquid up to about 3 metres.» What state of matter is the spray? | Ice | A gas that you can hold in a jar | *A liquid | A solid
test: «In a liquid like juice, the juice takes the shape of a tall glass but keeps the same amount.» What does a liquid take the shape of? | *Its container | The wind | Nothing, it has no shape | A shelf
test: How many main states of matter are there, in the lesson's list? | Two: liquid and gas | Four: hot, cold, warm and wet | *Three: solid, liquid and gas | One: water
exam: In which phrase is liquid used as an adjective? | A bottle of liquid | Liquids flow | *Liquid soap | The liquid's shape
